  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Adsorption is exothermic process due to decrease in surface energy. Micelle formation is endothermic, it is due to&nbsp;For any spontaneous process entropy should always increase, hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;S</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;for micelle formation and micelle formation decreases the stability of the colloidal solution so, energy of the mixture should increase which means&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p><p>The adsorption process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>ve</mi></math>. For micelle formation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>ve</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>ve</mi></math>.</p></blockquote>",
